⭐ Signature Items:
• Fried Potatoes, Shrimp &amp; Eggs: Thick-cut fried potatoes, massive pink shrimp, three jiggly fried eggs served in a hubcap-size cazuela (terra-cotta vessel); arrives on a wave of garlic-scented air; server punctures yolks tableside and tosses together; listed as appetizer but serves 2-3 as a main
• Suckling Pig: One roasted daily; can reserve entire animal two weeks ahead or order shoulder/leg portions à la minute; mild and unctuous, served with vinegary green salad and fries. Pig's head available upon request
• Jamón Ibérico: Ruby shavings of Spanish ham, silky and fat-streaked, served with puffy pan soplao (cracker-like bread imported from Spain's Panadería Jesús, photogenically printed with Bartolo logo)
🔥 Popular Items:
• Ajo Blanco: Creamy chilled Spanish almond soup adorned with delicate honeydew sorbet
• Torreznos con Almendras: Half-dozen Lego-size bricks of pork belly cooked to chicharrón crispiness, scattered with Marcona almonds; ideal bar snack with ginitonic
• Ginitonic: Briny gin and tonic garnished with an entire preserved lemon</description>
      <Point>
        <coordinates>-74.0039713,40.7372563,0</coordinates>
      </Point>
    </Placemark>
    <Placemark>
      <name>Laliko (West Village - Primary)</name>
      <description>Laliko - West Village (Primary)
📍 80 Carmine Street
📞 +1 917-388-3166
🔗 https://www.newyorker.com/culture/the-food-scene/a-georgian-restaurants-mother-of-all-dumplings
⭐ Signature Items:
• Mother Khinkali: An absurd, delightful, social-media-friendly mega-dumpling with the diameter and luminosity of a birthday-party balloon. A server presents an ornate silver dagger, pulls it from its curved sheath, and saws off the head to reveal a half-dozen standard-size dumplings nestled inside like &quot;tiny, steamy babies&quot; with freshly ground black pepper
• Khinkali (standard): Excellent steamed soup dumplings, plump and floppy, with springy dough rolled to porcelain thinness and pleasingly pleated twisted tops. Available in sets of four with fillings of soft lamb or mild cheese
• Khachapuri (Adjaruli): Open-faced boat of bread baked with an exorbitant amount of cheese, topped with egg yolk and butter, stirred together into a dairy-aisle gestalt
🔥 Popular Items:
• Georgian Wine: Indigenous varietals fermented in qvevri (large earthenware vessels buried underground), often with skin, seeds, stems. Amber Rkatsiteli with fruity and grassy notes; Tsinandali, white and apple-juicey
• Purple Plum Sauce: Side sauce that's puckery and sweet, bright and strange</description>
      <Point>
        <coordinates>-74.0048903,40.7294492,0</coordinates>
      </Point>
    </Placemark>
